    "buck": {
      "word": "BUCK",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "Lye or suds in which cloth is soaked in the operation of bleaching, or in which clothes are washed.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The cloth or clothes soaked or washed. [Obs.] Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "To soak, steep, or boil, in lye or suds; -- a process in bleaching.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To wash (clothes) in lye or suds, or, in later usage, by beating them on stones in running water.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Mining)",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To break up or pulverize, as ores.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "The male of deer, especially fallow deer and antelopes, or of goats, sheep, hares, and rabbits. pricket in his second; a sorel in his third; a sore in his fourth; a buck of the first head in his fifth; and a great buck in his sixth. The female of the fallow deer is termed a doe. The male of the red deer is termed a stag or hart and not a buck, and the female is called a hind. Brande & C.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A gay, dashing young fellow; a fop; a dandy. The leading bucks of the day. Thackeray.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A male Indian or negro. [Colloq. U.S.] antelopes; as, bush buck, spring buck. Blue buck. See under Blue. ellipsiprymnus). See Illust. of Antelope.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "To copulate, as bucks and does.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To spring with quick plunging leaps, descending with the fore legs rigid and the head held as low down as possible; -- said of a vicious horse or mule.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Mil.)",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To subject to a mode of punishment which consists in tying the wrists together, passing the arms over the bent knees, and putting a stick across the arms and in the angle formed by the knees.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To throw by bucking. See Buck, v. i., 2. The brute that he was riding had nearly bucked him out of the saddle. W. E. Norris.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "A frame on which firewood is sawed; a sawhorse; a sawbuck. Buck saw, a saw set in a frame and used for sawing wood on a sawhorse.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The beech tree. [Scot.] Buck mast, the mast or fruit of the beech tree. Johnson.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        }
      ],
